    <h2>My Daily Routine</h2>

    <p>-I believe that having a daily routine helps me stay organized, productive, and healthy. Every day, I balance my
        studies, responsibilities, family time, relaxation, and spiritual growth.</p>

    <ol>
        <li><b>6:00 AM - Wake Up</b>
            <p>I wake up early, thank God for a new day, make my bed, brush my teeth, take a shower, and get dressed in
                my
                school uniform.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>6:30 AM - Breakfast</b>
            <p>I enjoy a healthy breakfast to give me energy for the day ahead.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>6:45 AM - Prepare for School</b>
            <p>I pack my school bag, check that I have all my books and stationery, and get ready to leave for school.
            </p>
        </li>

        <li><b>7:00 AM - Travel to School</b>
            <p>I leave for school feeling excited to learn something new.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>7:30 AM - 3:00 PM - School</b>
            <p>At school, I attend lessons, complete classwork, participate in activities, and spend time with my
                friends.
                My favourite subjects include Mathematics, Physics, Accounting, Economics, Business Studies, English,
                and
                ICT.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>3:00 PM - Relax</b>
            <p>After arriving home, I spend one hour relaxing. I may eat a snack, watch television, or play games to
                refresh
                my mind after school.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>4:00 PM - 6:00 PM - Productive Learning</b>
            <p>I spend two hours doing activities that exercise my brain. I may revise school work, practise
                Mathematics,
                improve my coding skills, read books, or learn something new online. During this time, I take two to
                four
                short breaks of about ten minutes each.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>6:00 PM - Help Prepare Dinner</b>
            <p>I help my mother prepare dinner. Cooking together teaches me responsibility and allows me to learn
                something
                new every day.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>6:45 PM - Visit the Temple</b>
            <p>I visit the temple until 8:00 PM, where I pray, reflect, attend spiritual classes and thank God for His
                blessings.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>8:00 PM - Dinner</b>
            <p>I enjoy dinner with my family.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>8:15 PM - Household Chores</b>
            <p>After dinner, I help wash the dishes and clean the kitchen.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>8:30 PM - Homework</b>
            <p>I spend about thirty minutes completing my homework and revising what I learned at school.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>9:00 PM - Prepare for Tomorrow</b>
            <p>I pack my school bag, arrange my school uniform, and make sure everything is ready for the next day.</p>
        </li>

        <li><b>9:15 PM - Bedtime</b>
            <p>Before sleeping, I think about my day and thank God for His guidance, blessings, and protection. Then I
                go to
                sleep, ready for another day of my life.</p>
        </li>
    </ol>

